{"category": "manualAnswer", "expect": {"calls": [], "readingAccepted": true}, "group": "fieldAssist", "id": "sv-004-answer", "offered": [], "passages": {"p1": "Manifold pressure and operating pressure signal (Delta P) — TABLE 39 SM p.67, TABLE 35 II p.64\nManifold pressure is a differential: \"+\" on the manifold tap on the outlet side of the gas valve, \"-\" teed into the gas valve regulator vent hose (adapter kit 10L34). Delta P is taken across the positive and negative lines between the gas valve and the pressure switch. Run low heat (35%) for 5 minutes before reading, then repeat on high heat. Natural gas should burn blue and the flame should not lift. Valid 0–7,500 ft. Nameplate values for reference: 3.5 in. w.g. natural / 10.0 LP at maximum input, 0.5 / 1.5 at minimum input (SM p.2).\n| Firing rate | Manifold, natural gas | Manifold, LP/propane | Operating pressure signal (Delta P) |\n| Low, all models except 090XV60C | 0.40 – 0.95 | 1.2 – 2.8 | 0.20 – 0.40 |"}, "reading": {"answer": "Low, all models except 090XV60C, manifold, natural gas: 0.40 – 0.95 in. w.c..", "found": true, "passage": "p1", "quote": "Low, all models except 090XV60C | 0.40 – 0.95 | 1.2 – 2.8 | 0.20 – 0.40"}, "source": "service_values.md", "turn": "Manifold pressure and operating pressure signal: what should the manifold, natural gas be for Low, all models except 090XV60C?", "vault": "lennox-slp99"}
