{"category": "manualAnswer", "expect": {"calls": [], "readingAccepted": true}, "group": "fieldAssist", "id": "cal-01-answer", "offered": [], "passages": {"p1": "Manifold pressure and operating pressure signal (Delta P) — TABLE 39 SM p.67, TABLE 35 II p.64\nManifold pressure is a differential: \"+\" on the manifold tap on the outlet side of the gas valve, \"-\" teed into the gas valve regulator vent hose (adapter kit 10L34). Delta P is taken across the positive and negative lines between the gas valve and the pressure switch. Run low heat (35%) for 5 minutes before reading, then repeat on high heat. Natural gas should burn blue and the flame should not lift. Valid 0–7,500 ft. Nameplate values for reference: 3.5 in. w.g. natural / 10.0 LP at maximum input, 0.5 / 1.5 at minimum input (SM p.2).\n| Firing rate | Manifold, natural gas | Manifold, LP/propane | Operating pressure signal (Delta P) |\n| High, all models | 3.0 – 3.8 | 9.1 – 10.5 | 0.95 – 1.25 |"}, "reading": {"answer": "Manifold, natural gas: 3.0 – 3.8 in. w.c. on high fire.", "found": true, "passage": "p1", "quote": "High, all models | 3.0 – 3.8"}, "source": "eval/calibration.jsonl", "turn": "What is the manifold pressure on high fire?", "vault": "lennox-slp99"}
{"category": "manualAnswer", "expect": {"calls": [], "readingAccepted": true}, "group": "fieldAssist", "id": "cal-02-answer", "offered": [], "passages": {"p1": "Gas supply (line) pressure — TABLE 34, SM p.64\nMeasured at the supply pressure tap on the inlet side of the gas valve, unit firing at maximum rate. Supply piping must not drop more than 0.5 in. w.c. between meter and unit.\n| Gas | Line pressure, in. w.c. |\n| Natural | 4.5 – 10.5 |"}, "reading": {"answer": "Natural gas line pressure: 4.5 – 10.5 in. w.c., at the supply tap on the inlet side.", "found": true, "passage": "p1", "quote": "Natural | 4.5 – 10.5"}, "source": "eval/calibration.jsonl", "turn": "How do I measure the gas supply pressure at the valve?", "vault": "lennox-slp99"}
{"category": "manualAnswer", "expect": {"calls": [], "readingAccepted": true}, "group": "fieldAssist", "id": "cal-03-answer", "offered": [], "passages": {"p1": "Flame signal — TABLE 39 II p.64\nRead in Field Test mode on the seven-segment display. Normal 2.6 µA or greater; low 2.5 or less; drop-out 1.1 µA. A much higher reading (15, for example) may appear and is not a fault. The flame sensor is on the left of the burner support, tip in the left-most burner's flame; it can be removed without disturbing the burners."}, "reading": {"answer": "Normal is 2.6 µA or greater.", "found": true, "passage": "p1", "quote": "Normal 2.6 µA or greater"}, "source": "eval/calibration.jsonl", "turn": "What flame signal in microamps should I read at the sensor?", "vault": "lennox-slp99"}
